  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a860c39d3bee20a4dbf1652f7a813971, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The archive on the hill. Three readers today. One will not return.
    midDaysAnswer: The rare books vault. The smog gets into the bindings. I sealed what I could.
    finalDaysAnswer: The library. I still unlock it each morning. No one comes.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: The school on Chavchavadze Street. Twenty years teaching children literature.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Home. My husband keeps the stove going while I read.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The archive? It closed years ago. I haven't been since.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: None. I sleep well. Though I dreamt something I had no right to know.
    midDaysAnswer: Cold hands, for weeks now. The headaches arrive before the weather does.
    finalDaysAnswer: I tire quickly. The archive stairs take longer. All as I expected.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing. Past sixty, a little stiffness. Nothing more than that.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Warm hands, clear head. I have no idea what tomorrow holds.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing now. The doctor forbade me the archive stairs, so I rest.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I read one page three times. It said something different each time.
    - That window behind you. I would not stand so close to it.
    midDays:
    - You look tired. Sleep while you still dream things worth dreaming.
    - I would not touch the ink today. It smells different than yesterday.
    finalDays:
    - Your ending is very close now. It reads quite peacefully, I assure you.
    - I've already read past this part. You needn't know what happens next.
